    ["DictKey_sortie_1"] = "Operation Overwatch",
    ["DictKey_descriptionText_1"] = "Operation Overwatch - close air support over Kandahar and Helmand provinces, 23 September 2010, during Operation Dragon Strike.\n\nCoalition ground forces are in contact with insurgents across the green zones of the Arghandab and Helmand rivers. Fly from Kandahar Airfield, or from FARP Pasab (Zhari) and FARP Gereshk in the AH-64D and OH-58D.\n\nAfter takeoff, use F10 > Check In for a new CAS tasking, or F10 > Join Tasking to work an active one. Contact the JTAC on the tasking's frequency for the situation, target description, and marks. Expect small arms, RPGs, DShK and ZU-23 fire, and possible MANPADS. Avoid fratricide: friendlies cannot see the shooters and the JTAC's smoke marks the approximate enemy position.\n\nCheck-in point: Highway 1 halfway between Kandahar and Camp Bastion.\n\n=== COMMUNICATIONS PLAN ===\n\nCH   NAME           FREQ\n1    Strike         255.1\n2    SkyEye GCI     255.3\n3    Kandahar TWR   254.1\n4    Kandahar GND   254.3\n5    Kandahar RDR   254.5\n6    Tanker         270.5 Texaco (F-16C, F-15E) / 270.7 Shell (A-10C) / 270.1 Arco (probe)\n7    Axeman JTAC    256.1\n8    Darknight JTAC 256.3\n9    Warrior JTAC   256.5\n10   Pointer JTAC   256.7\n11-15 Red 1-5       260.1-260.9\n16-18 Blue 1-3      261.1-261.5\n19   Guard          243.0\n20   Blue 4         261.7\n\nSecond V/UHF radios: ch1 SkyEye VHF 124.1, then the list above.\nA-10C ARC-186 and F-16C COMM2: ch1 SkyEye FM 32.1 (F-16C: ch1 124.1, ch2 32.1), Yellow 1-5 30.1-30.9 FM, Orange 1-5 31.1-31.9 FM.\nHelicopters: no presets yet; tune manually.\n\nSUPPORT\nTankers are stacked over the Registan, 50 km south of Highway 1. Hot legs fly east along x -300 km; return legs are to the south.\nTexaco 11  KC-135 boom        270.5  TACAN 100X  FL200 280 KIAS  z -160 to -90 km\nArco 11    KC-135MPRS drogue  270.1  TACAN 101X  FL180 250 KIAS  z -140 to -70 km\nShell 11   KC-135 slow boom   270.7  TACAN 102X  FL150 200 KIAS  z -150 to -80 km (A-10C)\nOverlord   E-3A datalink only. Voice GCI: SkyEye 255.3 / 124.1 / 32.1 FM\nFARP Pasab 127.5   FARP Gereshk 127.7\nLaser code 1688",
